{"agent":"recover-2i","data":{"by":"recover-2i","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_sh_c` returns the index of the `-c` word and `_commands` always takes `head[i + 1]` as the shell program. Bash reads the program from the first non-option argument after option parsing, and option arguments are not that word. `bash -co pipefail 'git push origin main'` runs `git push` (`c` is `-c`, `pipefail` is the `-o` optarg), but `last` stays on `-co` and the inspected string is `pipefail`, so `check` returns None. The same miss happens for `bash -c -x 'git push origin main'` (payload taken is `-x`) and `bash -c -- 'git push origin main'` / `bash -c - 'git push origin main'` (payload taken is `--` or `-`; a lone `-` is end-of-options, which this loop skips and continues past). A `c` in a `+` cluster is also treated as `-c`, so `bash +c 'git push origin main'` is refused even though that word is a script name, not a `-c` program.","digest":"f4ebc55c59b4d995","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_sh_c","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_sh_c"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"3/4 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"e34fc7e4fb3fe29269e9be555ec724b12f40a740ca5ed928e4723c14141c52a8","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_chars":8000,"output_digest":"c237acdd1f434661","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261109T022041Z-eb7cd2a5.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,3,4],"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"dc2fd93a7e33+clean","wanted":[1,2,3,4]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 3 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 3, 4); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"eeb901b4465de3a5a216b7809","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":158503,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-forbidden-